@@ -3,3 +3,22 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of a parsed JSON
+document that a JSON Pointer refers to:
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1
+resolvePointer(document, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is invalid (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be
+followed by `0` or `1`), or when it does not resolve to a value: missing member, array index out of
+range or not canonical (`01`, `-1`), the `-` token (the element past the end of an array), or a step
+into a primitive. Only the string form is supported, not the URI fragment form (`#/foo`). Inherited
+properties such as `toString` are never resolved.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs TypeScript directly).
